			"notes": "### New\n- **Players, mobs and items in front of a display get its light.** An entity gets the light where it stands, as bright and as colored as a wall there facing the picture would get, shadows included.\n  - Its light level rises with the display's brightness.\n  - Players and mobs take on the light's color, together with everything they wear (armor, capes, elytra), as strongly as the display's share of all the light there.\n  - Your own first-person hand too. Held items keep their own colors.\n  - `entityLight` in the settings turns it off.\n\n### Downloads\nPick the jar for your Minecraft version:\n\n| Minecraft | File |\n|---|---|\n| 26.3 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.3+26.3.jar` |\n| 26.2 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.3+26.2.jar` |\n| 26.1.2 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.3+26.1.2.jar` |\n| 1.21.11 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.3+1.21.11.jar` |\n| 1.21.1 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.3+1.21.1.jar` |\n| 1.20.1 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.3+1.20.1.jar` |\n| 1.19.4 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.3+1.19.4.jar` |\n| 1.18.2 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.3+1.18.2.jar` |\n\n### Requirements\n- Fabric Loader 0.19.5+ and Fabric API\n- Dream Displays 1.10.6+ (client)\n- Optional: Sodium + Iris, LambDynamicLights (1.20.1 and newer), [Dream Displays Beam](https://github.com/XCraftTM/dreamdisplays-beam) 0.2.1+ (casts light the room too)\n\nClient-only: servers only need Dream Displays itself."
