			"notes": "### Fixed\n- **The blocks right in front of a screen are lit.** The row of floor (or wall) along the picture stayed dark: the light came from a hair in front of the picture, so the blocks right at it saw it edge-on. Most visible with a screen standing on the floor.\n- **Zone colors blend smoothly in front of the screen** instead of lighting the floor in hard-edged tiles one zone wide (4 blocks on an 8 block wide screen).\n- **Displays more than one block deep** light from the picture itself, where Dream Displays draws it, not from the front of their whole block box.\n- Each zone now lights as the rectangle it is, so the light right in front of the picture is as bright as a screen that close is; further away it is the same as before.\n\n### Other\n- Light rebuilds that take a quarter second or more are logged.\n\n### Downloads\nPick the jar for your Minecraft version:\n\n| Minecraft | File |\n|---|---|\n| 26.3 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.2+26.3.jar` |\n| 26.2 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.2+26.2.jar` |\n| 26.1.2 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.2+26.1.2.jar` |\n| 1.21.11 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.2+1.21.11.jar` |\n| 1.21.1 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.2+1.21.1.jar` |\n| 1.20.1 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.2+1.20.1.jar` |\n| 1.19.4 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.2+1.19.4.jar` |\n| 1.18.2 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.2+1.18.2.jar` |\n\n### Requirements\n- Fabric Loader 0.19.5+ and Fabric API\n- Dream Displays 1.10.6+ (client)\n- Optional: Sodium + Iris, LambDynamicLights (1.20.1 and newer), [Dream Displays Beam](https://github.com/XCraftTM/dreamdisplays-beam) 0.2.1+ (casts light the room too)\n\nClient-only: servers only need Dream Displays itself."
		},
