			"notes": "### New\n- **Pictures other mods draw on a display light the room too**, such as [Dream Displays Beam](https://github.com/XCraftTM/dreamdisplays-beam)'s screen and camera casts (Beam 0.2.1+). While such a picture is shown, its colors count instead of the display's own video, and the display lights even when it has no video.\n- For mod authors: `dev.xcrafttm.ddlumen.api.LumenFrames.submit(display, rgba, width, height)` on the render thread for each new frame, `end(display)` when the picture is gone.\n\n### Downloads\nPick the jar for your Minecraft version:\n\n| Minecraft | File |\n|---|---|\n| 26.3 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.1+26.3.jar` |\n| 26.2 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.1+26.2.jar` |\n| 26.1.2 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.1+26.1.2.jar` |\n| 1.21.11 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.1+1.21.11.jar` |\n| 1.21.1 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.1+1.21.1.jar` |\n| 1.20.1 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.1+1.20.1.jar` |\n| 1.19.4 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.1+1.19.4.jar` |\n| 1.18.2 | `dreamdisplays-lumen-0.1.1+1.18.2.jar` |\n\n### Requirements\n- Fabric Loader 0.19.5+ and Fabric API\n- Dream Displays 1.10.6+ (client)\n- Optional: Sodium + Iris, LambDynamicLights (1.20.1 and newer)\n\nClient-only: servers only need Dream Displays itself."
